=== apt-mark ===
DESCRIPTION ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
apt 2.8.3 (arm64)

apt-mark is a simple command line interface for marking packages as manually
or automatically installed. It can also be used to manipulate the dpkg(1)
selection states of packages, and to list all packages with or without a
certain marking.


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  apt-mark [options] {auto|manual} pkg1 [pkg2 ...]


POSITIONALS (2) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  {auto|manual}
                   values: auto, manual
  pkg...

=== apt-mark auto ===
Mark the given packages as automatically installed

=== apt-mark manual ===
Mark the given packages as manually installed

=== apt-mark minimize-manual ===
Mark all dependencies of meta packages as automatically installed.

=== apt-mark hold ===
Mark a package as held back

=== apt-mark unhold ===
Unset a package set as held back

=== apt-mark showauto ===
Print the list of automatically installed packages

=== apt-mark showmanual ===
Print the list of manually installed packages

=== apt-mark showhold ===
Print the list of packages on hold
